{
 "title": "AI doesn't see letters",
 "captions": [
  {
   "text": "AI doesn't !read words.!",
   "say": "A.I. doesn't read words.",
   "hide": true
  },
  {
   "text": "It reads *this.*"
  },
  {
   "text": "Before a language model sees your message,"
  },
  {
   "text": "it chops the text into *tokens:*"
  },
  {
   "text": "common chunks of letters, each turned into a *number.*"
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Strawberry\" might become *three pieces,*",
   "say": "Strawberry might become three pieces,"
  },
  {
   "text": "like *\"str\",* *\"aw\"* and *\"berry\".*",
   "say": "like, ess tee ar, eh double-you, and berry."
  },
  {
   "text": "The model !never! sees the individual letters."
  },
  {
   "text": "So when you ask how many R's it has,",
   "say": "So when you ask how many arrs it has,"
  },
  {
   "text": "it's reasoning about *chunks,* !not spelling.!"
  },
  {
   "text": "Newer models often *work around this,*"
  },
  {
   "text": "but the letters were !never! what it saw."
  }
 ],
